        The bug was caused by the system returning LE flow credits to the sender even when the socket's receive buffer was full, which led to a lack of back-pressure on the sender. This resulted in the sender continuing to send data, causing data loss without any error being reported. The fixed implementation now computes the number of returned LE flow credits based on the estimated available space in the receive buffer, preventing credits from being sent when the buffer is full.

